WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.700
- [Narrator] And as they
approached the finish line.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:03.533
- Two, three, four.

00:00:03.533 --> 00:00:04.890
- [Narrator] It seemed as if the cast

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:07.041
and crew were having
the time of their lives.

00:00:07.041 --> 00:00:07.874
(record scratching)

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:08.707
Weren't they?

00:00:08.707 --> 00:00:10.194
- We have to shoot the finale.

00:00:10.194 --> 00:00:12.310
- The night before we were shooting.

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:14.963
- They sent us another
paper bag full of cassettes.

00:00:14.963 --> 00:00:17.750
- All original songs
that had been submitted.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.705
- [Narrator] Jimmy had delivered
on the old classic songs,

00:00:19.705 --> 00:00:21.290
but he was cutting

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:23.910
the original finale
song they needed close.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:26.290
- And we were taking these
cassettes out of the bag

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:28.549
one at a time and listening to them.

00:00:28.549 --> 00:00:31.145
Pop, take it out, next one.

00:00:31.145 --> 00:00:34.214
The last cassette.

00:00:34.214 --> 00:00:36.047
- It starts off (vocalizes).

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:41.017
- And I stopped it and I said,

00:00:41.017 --> 00:00:46.017
"Miranda, is it because it's
the last friggin' cassette

00:00:46.607 --> 00:00:49.420
"or is there something in
the lyric of this song?"

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:50.481
And she said.

00:00:50.481 --> 00:00:51.317
- "Put it in."

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:52.205
- "Put it on again."

00:00:52.205 --> 00:00:53.812
♪ Now I'm ♪

00:00:53.812 --> 00:00:56.240
♪ Having the time of my life ♪

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.714
- Oh my god, maybe that's the song.

00:00:58.714 --> 00:01:00.218
- Well, that was it.

00:01:00.218 --> 00:01:03.038
- [Narrator] And for the
next three days straight

00:01:03.038 --> 00:01:05.920
it was all they heard.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:08.846
A cast of hundreds, endless dancing,

00:01:08.846 --> 00:01:11.490
working late into the night.

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:13.896
- We were doing it into,
like, three in the morning.

00:01:13.896 --> 00:01:15.703
- [Woman] Hi, Mom.

00:01:15.703 --> 00:01:16.547
- Hi, Mom.

00:01:16.547 --> 00:01:17.394
- Hi, Mom.

00:01:17.394 --> 00:01:18.700
- [Narrator] And they
also filmed that line

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:21.898
that might well be more
famous than the movie itself.

00:01:21.898 --> 00:01:23.520
- Nobody puts Baby in a corner.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:24.855
- Nobody puts Baby in a corner.

00:01:24.855 --> 00:01:26.550
- What a ridiculous line.

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:28.370
- There was no corner we were shooting in.

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:29.392
There's kind of a pillar.

00:01:29.392 --> 00:01:31.870
- [Narrator] But the line's
author must surely have seen

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:34.090
that immortal phrase as she penned

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:35.993
that unforgettable dialogue.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:40.293
- I think it's really something

00:01:40.293 --> 00:01:43.300
that I was not deeply committed to.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.290
I don't think it's a great phrase.

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:46.790
- [Narrator] Okay then, how 'bout the guy

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:48.670
who acted it into a great phrase?

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:50.590
- He thought it was the
stupidest line in the world

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:51.440
and I think he was right.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:52.457
- Years later he said,

00:01:52.457 --> 00:01:54.185
"Boy, was I wrong about that one!"

00:01:54.185 --> 00:01:55.730
- [Narrator] But it wasn't just

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:58.010
a painful line Patrick had to endure.

00:01:58.010 --> 00:01:59.130
The finale had some of

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:01.930
the most technically difficult
dancing in the movie.

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:04.380
- When he jumps off the
stage and does that tour.

00:02:06.936 --> 00:02:08.528
- He really busted up his knee.

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:09.413
- [Director] Here we go.

00:02:09.413 --> 00:02:10.290
One more time, please.

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:14.260
- He had to leap off that
stage 12 or 13, 14 times.

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.460
- [Director] Here we go.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.290
- He was hurting.

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:19.763
- [Director] Once again.

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:26.152
- And he came over to me
and he whispered in my ear,

00:02:26.152 --> 00:02:29.187
"I've got one more in me.

00:02:29.187 --> 00:02:32.710
"Please make sure all the cameras get it."

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:36.077
Then I said to Emil, "We
have to get it right now.

00:02:36.077 --> 00:02:37.547
"Patrick's suffering.

00:02:37.547 --> 00:02:40.761
"He wants to do this but we
have to get it at this moment."

00:02:40.761 --> 00:02:42.330
- Let's do one more shot.

00:02:43.174 --> 00:02:44.221
- I'll stand by.

00:02:44.221 --> 00:02:47.882
- [Director] Three, two, and playback.

00:02:47.882 --> 00:02:50.632
(dramatic music)

00:02:52.329 --> 00:02:53.172
Cut!

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:55.387
(cheering)

00:02:55.387 --> 00:02:57.270
- He had one more in him.

00:02:57.270 --> 00:02:58.660
He was that kind of a person.

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:00.948
He suffered for his art.

00:03:00.948 --> 00:03:03.720
- [Narrator] But Patrick wasn't done yet.

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:05.800
The finale wouldn't be complete

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:10.694
without one iconic moment and
one last show of strength.

00:03:10.694 --> 00:03:15.694
(dramatic music)
(chattering)

00:03:25.563 --> 00:03:27.813
(cheering)

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:35.172
After 45 days, those splendid words.

00:03:35.172 --> 00:03:36.855
- [Director] That's a wrap.

00:03:36.855 --> 00:03:39.188
(cheering)

